// Original author - Jake Holland
//
// @input.value - The value to check.
//
// @desc A basic type check function to see if a value can be translated into a valid array from JSON.
//
// @depends none
// @returns boolean - True or false depending on the result of the type check.
//
// WARNING: As this function can only return a string in CRM
// the return value will have to be checked after converting
// to a boolean like this:
// standalone.is_array(value) == "true"
//
// set as a value of a map and then strip the surrounding map from the value
// NOTE: This normalises actual deluge list varialbes into JSON notation.
// Calling toString on a list in deluge wont surround the list with a square
// brackets as we would expect in a JSON array.
map_value = {"value":value};
map_value = map_value.toString();
translated_value = map_value.subString(9);
translated_value = translated_value.subString(0,translated_value.length() - 1);
//
// check if array is potentially stringified
first_character = IF(translated_value.length() > 0,translated_value.subString(0,1),null);
if(first_character == "\"")
{
	translated_value = translated_value.removeFirstOccurence("\"");
	translated_value = translated_value.removeLastOccurence("\"");
}
//
// check surrounding characters
// NOTE: When the first and last character are a bracket we will treat it as a valid
// array value because it should be possible to parse as a JSON array.
first_character = IF(translated_value.length() > 0,translated_value.subString(0,1),null);
last_character = IF(translated_value.length() > 0,translated_value.subString(translated_value.length() - 1),null);
if(first_character == "[" && last_character == "]")
{
	return true;
}
//
// must not be an array
return false;
